{
  "schema_version": 1.0,
  "name": "Saltpan Crossing",
  "description": "A tidal flat where shallow water covers most of the ground. A few dry hummocks rise above the waterline; a single elevated causeway of dry ground runs the length of the map. Movement through the shallows is slow but always possible; the causeway is the express route. Hold the causeway, but the hummocks are where the resources are.",
